1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:02,800
Well, my family has a mystical lineage.

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:05,240
<i>Remember that I'll always be by your side.</i>

3
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:06,680
<i>From now on, let's be "F."</i>

4
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:08,240
Friends with benefits.

5
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,240
<i>Thank you.</i>

6
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:12,240
<i>I only made it through the difficult time</i>
<i>because of you.</i>

7
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,960
<i>I think we can officially be</i>
<i>in the talking stage now.</i>

8
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,080
You don't need to win me over anymore.

9
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:25,160
<i>Khobfa, hurry up.</i>

10
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:28,120
<i>Come on, stand in the middle.</i>
<i>That's right.</i>

11
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,080
One, two…

12
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:32,640
Whoa, you look like a statue.

13
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:34,480
We're not taking an ID photo. Hold this.

14
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,600
Yeah, try to look natural.

15
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:39,000
Do we really need to do it like this?

16
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,400
Of course.

17
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:42,760
This is a poster
to recruit new band members.

18
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:45,040
If the photos aren't appealing,
who'll apply?

19
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:47,520
But I don't like competitions.
I don't like competing.

20
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,320
You don't have to think of it that way.

21
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:52,000
Just get onstage, play,
and let people hear your music.

22
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:57,240
If no one ever hears a good song,
can it really be called a good song?

23
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:58,160
Right?

24
00:00:58,240 --> 00:00:59,360
Not necessarily.

25
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:01,560
There are plenty of great songs
that hardly anyone listens to.

26
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:04,040
Whatever. Come on.

27
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:05,920
<i>One, two.</i>

28
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,440
Let's try another pose.

29
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:10,360
Lift the guitar like this.
Rest it on your shoulder.

30
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:11,920
Yeah, just like that.

31
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,760
And smile.

32
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:16,400
If you don't smile in this pose,
you'll look intimidating.

33
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:18,200
Smile.
People might be too scared to apply.

34
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:20,600
<i>One, two, three.</i>

35
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:25,320
This one looks great.

36
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:27,160
Don't you think I'm smiling too much?

37
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:31,720
Too much? No. It's barely a smile.

38
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:34,360
Or do you prefer this?

39
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:35,480
This one's good.

40
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:38,480
You look like you're mad at someone.

41
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:41,600
You need to smile like this. Like this.

42
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,680
THE GRANDEST CONTEST OF OUR UNIVERSITY

43
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:49,600
Do you think anyone will join my band?

44
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,720
Of course. Someone will.

45
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:55,240
And if no one does,

46
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,960
we'll find a way to make it happen.

47
00:02:57,200 --> 00:03:00,600
Hey, people are encouraging us
to form a band for the university contest.

48
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:04,040
Yeah, one of the seniors asked me
to convince you to enter.

49
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,920
He said it'd make
this year's contest more exciting.

50
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:13,080
That does sound interesting.
If I apply, will you help me?

51
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:20,640
Try begging me cutely.
Maybe you'll win me over.

52
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:33,600
Little Mochi, would you please
consider accepting me, Krit?

53
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:36,080
I'll think about it.

54
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,560
Really?

55
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:40,560
I don't know.

56
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:42,880
DAD

57
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,400
I'll be right back.

58
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:03,520
GRANDMA

59
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:09,680
GRANDMA

60
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:17,160
GRANDMA

61
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:26,920
Your grandma called you so many times.
Are you really not going to answer?

62
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,040
Hi, Grandma.

63
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:51,600
<i>Khobfa, how have you been?</i>
<i>Are you doing okay?</i>

64
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:54,160
<i>Come visit me this weekend, dear.</i>

65
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:57,800
I'll probably be busy with work.

66
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:59,560
<i>Really?</i>

67
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:03,080
<i>You can bring your work and do it here.</i>
<i>I miss you.</i>

68
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:04,800
I also…

69
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:10,760
If I finish my work, I'll go and see you.

70
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:13,480
<i>All right. I'll be waiting.</i>

71
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,480
Okay.

72
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,520
Come on.
Let's continue checking our photos.

73
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,880
Let me take a break for a while.

74
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:43,560
My dad called to remind me
about dinner at home.

75
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:47,360
But something feels strange this time.

76
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:51,720
What's strange about it?
It's a good thing your dad called.

77
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,480
He told me to invite you too.

78
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:21,360
This is the plant you told me
you brought from your grandma's, right?

79
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,200
Yeah.

80
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:31,320
No wonder you take such good care of it.

81
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,840
If you miss your grandma,
why don't you go see her?

82
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,400
I think…

83
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:54,320
she deserves to know
how much you miss her.

84
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:01,960
You too.

85
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:09,240
You have every right to miss her too.

86
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:13,560
But I'm scared.

87
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,440
I'm really scared.

88
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:27,000
KHUNKAO CHAIPANHA
MAR 6, 1980-JAN 12, 2020

89
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:37,280
Have you decided
where you're going to live?

90
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,800
What do you mean?

91
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:41,760
You got accepted, didn't you?

92
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:44,880
Move somewhere near campus and…

93
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,760
Just don't come back here.

94
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,320
What do you mean?

95
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:58,160
Do you want Grandma to die
like your parents did?

96
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:04,760
You're bad luck.

97
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,840
Everyone around you ends up suffering.

98
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,520
The fortune teller warned us about you.

99
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,480
But Mom and Dad said that wasn't true.

100
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,760
Then where are they now?

101
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,400
Where are they, huh?

102
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:16,160
If it weren't for you?

103
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,680
I'm sorry.

104
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:23,440
I…

105
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:28,280
If you really love Grandma,
don't ever come back to see her.

106
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:29,800
Do you understand?

107
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,280
I knew it.

108
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:55,560
Someone as kind as you
must have reasons for doing anything.

109
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:00,040
But your uncle
deserves a punch in the face.

110
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,880
No, a hundred punches.

111
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:03,480
Right in the face!

112
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:05,360
Gosh.

113
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:14,320
You once told me that,
whenever I'm by your side,

114
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,840
everything will work out, right?

115
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:21,480
Yeah. Why?

116
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:29,400
Then let's go see your grandma together.

117
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:50,800
Grandma, I'm here!

118
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,680
Khobfa!

119
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:12,960
How do I look?

120
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,200
You look good.

121
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,560
I'm not confident at all.

122
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:20,920
I've never met your family before.

123
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:25,280
I'm sure it'll be fine.

124
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,240
Dad just wants to get to know you.

125
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:30,880
Have you ever brought anyone
to meet your dad before?

126
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:32,800
No. You're the first.

127
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:34,000
Really?

128
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:37,440
You're the first person
he's ever asked me to bring home.

129
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:39,880
I'm nervous.

130
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:44,800
What do you think your dad will ask me?

131
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,080
What's your name?

132
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:54,280
My name is Rin.

133
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:57,080
What's your relationship with Khobfa?

134
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:03,320
Right now, we're--

135
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:05,640
- We're roommates.
- Ouch!

136
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,280
Yeah, just roommates.

137
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:11,760
I just learned that kids these days
call their partners "roommates."

138
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:16,480
No, ma'am. We're not dating. We're not.

139
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:21,920
We're in the talking stage,
but we're not together yet.

140
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:25,200
Then keep talking.

141
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:31,040
Talk while walking,
standing, or lying down.

142
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:34,960
Keep it up,
and Rin will eventually give in.

143
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:44,000
- Will you really give in?
- What?

144
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:49,360
I haven't seen Khobfa smile like this
in a very long time.

145
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:54,000
You must be the one who makes him smile.

146
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:57,240
Me?

147
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:11,320
<i>Yes.</i>

148
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:13,520
I was the one
who asked Krit to invite you.

149
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:23,240
Oh, thank you for inviting me.

150
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:26,240
Is there something
you wanted to discuss with me?

151
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:28,360
Nothing.

152
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:32,560
We just wanted to meet someone
our son is close to.

153
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:34,320
Right, honey?

154
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:35,920
Yes.

155
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,520
It's nice to finally meet you in person.

156
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:43,240
Until now, we had only seen you
in the clips Kong and Kan showed us.

157
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:45,440
What clips?

158
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:50,400
The clips from your campaign.

159
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,240
Oh, right.

160
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:56,920
We're running a campaign
to promote the university's image.

161
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,520
We also have a joint channel now
with over 100,000 followers.

162
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:01,960
Well…

163
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:03,560
That sounds interesting.

164
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:11,000
How long have you been living with Mochi?

165
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:17,280
<i>It's been two years</i>
<i>since my dad passed away.</i>

166
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:19,360
These are my parents.

167
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:28,000
Everyone in your family is good-looking.

168
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,120
Of course.

169
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:33,520
What? I was complimenting your parents.

170
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:36,760
Complimenting them
is basically complimenting me.

171
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:41,400
Mom, Dad, this is my future boyfriend.

172
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:45,000
What? You've gone too far.

173
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:50,400
Sir, ma'am, we'll see how it goes.
It'll probably take a long time.

174
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:52,240
- Not long.
- A long time.

175
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:53,920
- Not long.
- A long time.

176
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:54,840
No, it won't.

177
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:57,160
Hey!

178
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:03,200
Well, your room is pretty nice.

179
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:08,400
Whoa.

180
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:32,120
I DON'T WANT TO GO TO SCHOOL.
WHY DOESN'T ANYONE LIKE ME?

181
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,680
WHY DOES EVERYONE HAVE TO HATE ME?

182
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
<i>I don't want to be a jinx.</i>

183
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,560
<i>I don't want to be a jinx.</i>

184
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:42,080
<i>I don't want to be a jinx.</i>

185
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:43,760
<i>I don't want to be a jinx.</i>

186
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:48,240
<i>I don't want to be a jinx!</i>

187
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:58,200
<i>Mom and Dad said I was their gift.</i>

188
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:05,680
Here you go.

189
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:15,400
This one's for you.

190
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:20,360
Thank you.

191
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:25,040
This is for me?

192
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:26,680
Of course.

193
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:31,360
I invited you to dinner with my family,
so of course I got you a gift.

194
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:33,480
Thank you.

195
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:05,240
Krit, Kong, Kan,
could you get my things from upstairs?

196
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:09,280
Sure.

197
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:13,400
You don't have to go.

198
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:16,240
Let the three of them go.

199
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,440
Stay and keep us company.

200
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,280
<i>Of course, Grandma. Don't worry.</i>

201
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,360
I'll shape them as well as I can.

202
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:35,720
Let me see.

203
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:37,520
Here, Grandma. Look.

204
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:39,480
You're good at this.

205
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:43,720
Grandma, should I put them in these bowls?

206
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:45,960
Yes. Pick the pretty ones.

207
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:47,080
Okay.

208
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:55,720
Thank you, Rin,
for bringing Khobfa back to see me.

209
00:16:56,840 --> 00:17:00,240
It wasn't me.
Khobfa already wanted to visit you.

210
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:02,400
If you hadn't come…

211
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:06,240
he wouldn't have.

212
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:09,440
Khobfa has a hard time trusting people.

213
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:12,280
He had a bad experience at school,

214
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:16,560
so he quit basketball
and music altogether.

215
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:20,720
Khobfa used to be in a band?

216
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:22,680
Yes.

217
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:27,040
I see.

218
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:36,560
There's still so much about Khobfa
that I don't know.

219
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:45,000
I've got it, Dad. Where should I put it?

220
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:51,360
I have somewhere else to be,
so I'll excuse myself.

221
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:53,760
Goodbye.

222
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:12,320
Influencers sure are busy, aren't they?

223
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:16,080
Let him go. It's actually better.

224
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:18,080
Now it's just our family.

225
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:20,000
Come on. Let's eat.

226
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:32,040
KHUNKAO CHAIPANHA 1980-2020
NITTAYA CHAIPANHA 1980-2016

227
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:37,640
Sweet rice balls with egg.
Grandma and I made them for you.

228
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:43,880
Rin helped too.

229
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:50,280
Mom, Dad, please watch over Grandma.

230
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:56,840
Your parents are in heaven.

231
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:58,760
Don't bother them.

232
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:01,400
You're the one
who has to care for your grandma.

233
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:03,520
But I'm a jinx--

234
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,640
A gift.

235
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:10,440
You're your parents' gift,
just like you wrote in your diary.

236
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:20,520
I'm sorry. I happened to come across it.

237
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:32,920
But I'm sure your parents
felt the same way.

238
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:51,160
You've got it easy.

239
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:53,440
You made me pedal all the way here.
Now I have to pedal back.

240
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:56,160
I don't know how to ride a bike.

241
00:19:56,240 --> 00:19:58,160
You can ride a motorcycle, though.

242
00:19:58,240 --> 00:20:01,200
You rode on the back of mine,
and now I'm riding on the back of yours.

243
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,800
That makes us even, right?

244
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:03,880
Hey, Rin.

245
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:05,280
What?

246
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:09,600
It's raining.

247
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:12,800
So? What's there to be afraid of?

248
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:14,080
Shouldn't we find shelter?

249
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:17,440
Didn't you ever play in the rain as a kid?

250
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:18,760
It's so much fun.

251
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:20,800
Should we find shelter?

252
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:23,680
No. Let's play in the rain. It's fun.

253
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:27,040
Come on, lift your feet! Quick!

254
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:28,440
Rin! What the hell are you doing?

255
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:30,520
I told you.
Playing in the rain is awesome.

256
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:31,640
Hey!

257
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:37,200
This really is fun.

258
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:40,000
Yeah!

259
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,320
Hey.

260
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:59,320
Why don't you go change in the bathroom?

261
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:09,080
Why? Are you shy?

262
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:11,840
Come here. I'll take it off for you.

263
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:13,040
Hey, no need.

264
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:17,760
I can do it myself.

265
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:57,560
Do you want to shower with me?

266
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:17,880
Why are you here again?

267
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:19,600
Get out right now!

268
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:22,840
This is my house. What right do you have
to give it to Khobfa?

269
00:22:26,040 --> 00:22:27,200
Khobfa! Where are you?

270
00:22:27,280 --> 00:22:28,760
If I don't leave it to Khobfa,

271
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:30,320
then should I leave it to you?

272
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:34,760
You never cared about me all these years.
Why come making demands now?

273
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:37,440
Go. Get out!

274
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:40,560
You care more about your grandson
than you do your own son?

275
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:44,280
Have you gone senile?

276
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:46,320
Grandma is your mother too.

277
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:48,520
Show her some respect.

278
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:50,440
Who are you to lecture me?

279
00:22:51,040 --> 00:22:53,600
I'm not lecturing you.
I'm just warning you.

280
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:56,600
I warned you not to come back, didn't I?

281
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:59,800
What happened last time?
Grandma ended up in the hospital.

282
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,160
It was because of you.

283
00:23:06,680 --> 00:23:10,880
Grandma calls me to visit all the time.
I can't bring myself to say no to her.

284
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:12,360
You can't say no,

285
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:15,040
or are you hoping to get something?

286
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:17,600
Like you, Uncle?

287
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:21,720
How dare you speak to me like that?

288
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:24,200
Don't bring bad luck to my mom
like you did to your parents.

289
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:25,360
Stop it right now!

290
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:26,400
Isn't it true, Mom?

291
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:28,160
Everyone knows this kid is a jinx.

292
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:36,640
What?

293
00:23:36,720 --> 00:23:38,520
You want to punch me, you little shit?

294
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:39,480
That's enough!

295
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:43,680
What kind of adult
keeps reopening a kid's wounds like this?

296
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:47,320
Oh, so you're Khobfa's friend.

297
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:51,240
No wonder. You're both pieces of shit.

298
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:56,800
If you're this drunk, go home. Go!

299
00:23:56,880 --> 00:23:58,200
Mind your fucking business!

300
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:07,000
Hey!

301
00:24:07,080 --> 00:24:09,000
Don't you dare touch my man.

302
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:11,760
Let go of me!

303
00:24:11,840 --> 00:24:13,320
That hurts!

304
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:15,440
Khobfa, that's enough.

305
00:24:27,720 --> 00:24:29,080
I'll go now, Grandma.

306
00:24:30,520 --> 00:24:32,440
Khobfa!

307
00:24:32,520 --> 00:24:34,080
Go wherever the hell you want, bastard.

308
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:35,760
- Khobfa, come back!
- Don't ever come back!

309
00:24:36,360 --> 00:24:39,920
Khobfa, how long will you keep
running away from your problems?

310
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:44,440
Seriously, how long will you let people
look down on you like this?

311
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:47,240
That's because I really am a jinx!

312
00:24:48,880 --> 00:24:50,960
Listen to me.

313
00:24:51,520 --> 00:24:53,200
You haven't had any bad luck at all.

314
00:24:53,800 --> 00:24:55,680
You haven't done anything wrong.

315
00:24:57,040 --> 00:24:59,080
You're not me. What would you know?

316
00:25:00,880 --> 00:25:02,280
Why wouldn't I know?

317
00:25:06,840 --> 00:25:08,840
Because you're lucky.

318
00:25:08,920 --> 00:25:11,120
Everyone loves and admires you.

319
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:13,120
You weren't born a jinx like me!

320
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:16,160
You think I've never had bad luck, huh?

321
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:20,960
<i>Mom, I won another award.</i>
<i>I'll bring it home to show you.</i>

322
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:23,320
- Don't run, sweetie. You'll fall.
- Dad!

323
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,680
- Hurry.
- Walk slowly.

324
00:25:24,760 --> 00:25:26,120
What do you want to play?

325
00:25:26,200 --> 00:25:29,200
You think someone who was lied to
his whole life about his dad being dead,

326
00:25:29,280 --> 00:25:32,080
only to learn he'd run off
to start a happier family,

327
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:34,600
<i>leaving his wife and son behind</i>
<i>with this stupid curse…</i>

328
00:25:39,520 --> 00:25:42,600
You think that's what happens
to someone who's lucky?

329
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:47,720
I'm sorry.

330
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:55,160
Forget it.

331
00:25:57,680 --> 00:25:59,120
It's good to let it out.

332
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:01,600
The same goes for you.

333
00:26:02,280 --> 00:26:04,000
You should let it out sometimes.

334
00:26:05,160 --> 00:26:06,880
Why do you keep bottling it all up?

335
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:12,200
Are you crazy? I'm a person, not a robot.

336
00:26:12,280 --> 00:26:14,200
I can't flip an emotion switch
like you can.

337
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:18,680
You can. You really can.

338
00:26:22,320 --> 00:26:23,640
I can't do it.

339
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:29,840
I know what to do.

340
00:26:30,440 --> 00:26:32,640
I'll take you somewhere
to blow off some steam.

341
00:26:33,640 --> 00:26:34,760
What?

342
00:26:43,440 --> 00:26:44,640
That's more like it.

343
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:46,680
Come on. I'll take you there.

344
00:26:59,080 --> 00:27:04,040
Okay, now that we're ready, pick one.

345
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:05,760
Which one?

346
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:10,040
Here. Let's go with this one.

347
00:27:11,800 --> 00:27:14,560
Now dip it into any color.

348
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:18,520
Think about the awful thing
that just happened,

349
00:27:18,600 --> 00:27:20,760
then splash it onto this.

350
00:27:23,560 --> 00:27:25,120
Here, I'll show you.

351
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:35,320
Just let it all out.

352
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:38,960
Everything bad, everything awful,
let it all out on here.

353
00:27:40,400 --> 00:27:41,280
Give it a try.

354
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:53,400
I'm not a jinx.
I didn't do anything wrong.

355
00:27:53,480 --> 00:27:55,640
I'm not a jinx.
I didn't do anything wrong.

356
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:57,880
I'm not a jinx!
I didn't do anything wrong!

357
00:27:57,960 --> 00:27:59,080
Yeah, that's it.

358
00:27:59,160 --> 00:28:00,720
Just like that.

359
00:28:01,320 --> 00:28:02,480
Now that's Khobfa!

360
00:28:02,560 --> 00:28:03,600
Now that's Rin!

361
00:28:07,160 --> 00:28:08,680
Khobfa!

362
00:28:08,760 --> 00:28:12,000
- Hey, relax!
- You're covered in green!

363
00:28:12,080 --> 00:28:13,400
Hey!

364
00:28:13,960 --> 00:28:15,000
<i>Whoa!</i>

365
00:28:21,480 --> 00:28:24,480
<i>Yes. Krit and I have been friends</i>
<i>since high school.</i>

366
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:28,280
But you only recently started
making couple content together?

367
00:28:28,880 --> 00:28:30,000
Yes.

368
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:38,480
I do support talented kids…

369
00:28:39,080 --> 00:28:43,280
from ordinary backgrounds.

370
00:28:45,920 --> 00:28:50,760
But honestly, this whole
couple-content thing you're doing

371
00:28:50,840 --> 00:28:52,280
isn't going to work.

372
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:54,640
You should stop.

373
00:28:56,080 --> 00:28:56,920
But Krit and I--

374
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,560
I've had someone look into you.

375
00:28:59,080 --> 00:29:01,280
You grew up in an orphanage, didn't you?

376
00:29:01,360 --> 00:29:05,000
Money must be important to you.

377
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:08,200
Name your price, and I'll pay it.

378
00:29:08,280 --> 00:29:10,520
But you have to stay away from my son.

379
00:29:18,800 --> 00:29:20,160
I've got it, Dad.

380
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:21,600
Where should I put it?

381
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:49,640
What made you call me here today?

382
00:29:51,360 --> 00:29:52,840
I just wanted to see you.

383
00:29:54,640 --> 00:29:56,280
Don't you have a boyfriend?

384
00:29:57,360 --> 00:29:58,480
Or did you get dumped?

385
00:30:00,880 --> 00:30:02,040
I'm single.

386
00:30:02,600 --> 00:30:06,520
We're just in the talking stage.

387
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:11,840
So…

388
00:30:14,080 --> 00:30:15,920
I still have a chance tonight, right?

389
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:21,960
KRIT

390
00:30:44,040 --> 00:30:48,560
Hey, Krit. Weren't you going to a bar?
I thought you were with Mochi.

391
00:30:49,080 --> 00:30:50,560
What bar?

392
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:54,480
Mochi posted a story.
I saw it and thought it was your hand.

393
00:30:57,080 --> 00:30:57,960
Look.

394
00:31:04,600 --> 00:31:06,440
I think Mochi hid his story from you.

395
00:31:11,120 --> 00:31:11,960
Huh?

396
00:31:15,600 --> 00:31:17,760
MS. DARAN

397
00:31:20,080 --> 00:31:21,040
Rin.

398
00:31:21,800 --> 00:31:22,640
Rin.

399
00:31:22,720 --> 00:31:23,640
Yeah?

400
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:24,920
Someone's calling you.

401
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:26,480
Who is it?

402
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:29,400
Ms. Daran.

403
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:31,000
Oh, really?

404
00:31:31,080 --> 00:31:32,680
- Yeah.
- Okay.

405
00:31:42,440 --> 00:31:44,080
Hello, Mom.

406
00:31:44,680 --> 00:31:45,920
Hello, Rin.

407
00:31:48,480 --> 00:31:50,960
How are you, son?
Did you move to a new place?

408
00:31:51,040 --> 00:31:52,840
Who are you living with?

409
00:31:53,560 --> 00:31:54,960
With Khobfa, Mom.

410
00:31:55,040 --> 00:31:57,800
Really? Can you trust him?

411
00:31:57,880 --> 00:32:00,160
Why aren't you staying with Danthai?

412
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:02,680
Did something happen between you two?

413
00:32:02,760 --> 00:32:05,760
Whoa, which question
should I answer first, Mom?

414
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:08,400
Nothing happened between Dan and me.

415
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:13,240
And as for Khobfa,
I trust him more than anyone.

416
00:32:13,320 --> 00:32:16,440
Is that so? Okay, that's great.

417
00:32:16,520 --> 00:32:20,720
The next time I'm back in Thailand,
don't forget to introduce him to me.

418
00:32:22,520 --> 00:32:24,800
Take care of yourself, okay?

419
00:32:24,880 --> 00:32:26,320
Wait, Mom.

420
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:29,640
Yes? What is it?

421
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:34,920
Nothing.

422
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:39,760
Thank you

423
00:32:40,520 --> 00:32:42,520
for being the kind of mother you are.

424
00:32:44,320 --> 00:32:48,560
Hey, what's this?
Why are you suddenly getting sentimental?

425
00:33:03,440 --> 00:33:05,000
I love you, Rin.

426
00:33:07,600 --> 00:33:09,000
I love you too, Mom.

427
00:33:10,320 --> 00:33:12,000
More than anyone in the world.

428
00:33:51,720 --> 00:33:53,600
My mom wants to meet you too.

429
00:33:54,200 --> 00:33:55,440
Really?

430
00:33:55,520 --> 00:33:56,440
Yeah.

431
00:33:57,200 --> 00:33:58,960
I want to meet her too.

432
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:02,440
Maybe I can ask you
to be my boyfriend in front of her.

433
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,000
Whoa, that's too much.

434
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:07,240
Boyfriend?

435
00:34:07,960 --> 00:34:09,960
Let's see how things go first.

436
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:15,040
Stop making that face. Forget it.

437
00:34:44,199 --> 00:34:47,199
I'm glad you opened up to me.

438
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:09,160
Hey!

439
00:35:22,600 --> 00:35:24,320
What the hell are you two doing?

440
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:26,960
Stay away from my boyfriend.

441
00:35:34,960 --> 00:35:36,200
We need to talk.

442
00:35:40,840 --> 00:35:42,320
What the hell are you doing?

443
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:44,000
That's what I should ask you.

444
00:35:44,080 --> 00:35:46,960
You've been avoiding me and lying to me.

445
00:35:47,040 --> 00:35:48,560
Why did you do that?

446
00:35:49,240 --> 00:35:51,000
What I do is none of your business.

447
00:35:51,080 --> 00:35:54,160
Don't forget we're just friends
with benefits. I'm not your boyfriend.

448
00:35:54,240 --> 00:35:55,360
I'm worried about you.

449
00:35:57,560 --> 00:36:01,000
You're acting like this
because of my dad, aren't you?

450
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:03,840
He told you to stop seeing me, didn't he?

451
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:07,200
Krit.

452
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:10,400
I know everything.

453
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:13,880
Who are you calling?

454
00:36:17,160 --> 00:36:20,160
Mochi. He won't answer.

455
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:23,400
Krit,

456
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:26,520
Dad asked you and Mochi to come today

457
00:36:27,280 --> 00:36:30,880
because he wanted Mochi
to stop seeing you.

458
00:36:39,040 --> 00:36:42,280
Didn't I tell you to tell me
if anything happened?

459
00:36:44,760 --> 00:36:46,840
I didn't want you
to have problems with your dad.

460
00:36:55,440 --> 00:36:56,520
Hello, Dad.

461
00:36:59,080 --> 00:37:01,640
You said you wanted all your children
to be happy, right?

462
00:37:03,800 --> 00:37:06,800
Well, Mochi and I are so damn happy.

463
00:37:08,600 --> 00:37:11,280
We're not going to break up
because of what you said.

464
00:37:13,840 --> 00:37:15,280
What the fuck are you doing?

465
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:19,600
You'll get into another fight
with your dad and end up hurt again.

466
00:37:24,480 --> 00:37:28,120
I'd be more hurt if I lost you.

467
00:37:56,560 --> 00:37:59,200
Do you really think
anyone will want to join our band?

468
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:01,160
Someone will.

469
00:38:01,240 --> 00:38:02,760
Look, I put up a new poster.

470
00:38:02,840 --> 00:38:04,800
Your application form is ready too.

471
00:38:05,440 --> 00:38:06,960
Just wait. Someone will show up.

472
00:38:07,040 --> 00:38:09,400
- But will this poster even help--
- Stop.

473
00:38:09,480 --> 00:38:13,000
Whatever you're thinking, don't say it.

474
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:17,320
Have some faith.

475
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:19,720
Hey, look. Excuse me!

476
00:38:19,800 --> 00:38:21,760
Are you interested in joining a band?

477
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:24,000
No, thanks.

478
00:38:28,240 --> 00:38:30,360
THE CAMPUS STAGE
BATTLE OF THE BANDS APPLICATION

479
00:38:31,120 --> 00:38:33,800
It's okay.
There are plenty of people around here.

480
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:42,840
Don't tell me
you're actually competing in this too.

481
00:38:45,680 --> 00:38:46,880
Let's go, Khobfa.

482
00:38:47,920 --> 00:38:49,680
There's still time to withdraw.

483
00:38:49,760 --> 00:38:50,600
Yeah.

484
00:38:50,680 --> 00:38:53,760
If you don't have a band,
you can't compete.

485
00:38:53,840 --> 00:38:56,720
I don't have one yet, but I will.

486
00:38:56,800 --> 00:38:58,480
Don't worry about losing so soon.

487
00:38:59,280 --> 00:39:02,360
Really? Well, good luck.

488
00:39:07,080 --> 00:39:08,760
Krit! Mochi!

489
00:39:08,840 --> 00:39:10,400
I'm interested. Where do I sign up?

490
00:39:10,480 --> 00:39:11,440
Right here.

491
00:39:12,760 --> 00:39:14,120
Move!

492
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:16,080
Scan it now.

493
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:20,000
- Done.
- Nice.

494
00:39:20,080 --> 00:39:21,360
Hurry.

495
00:39:24,040 --> 00:39:25,880
Hey, guys.

496
00:39:26,440 --> 00:39:27,480
What are you doing?

497
00:39:30,920 --> 00:39:32,520
HORIZON IS LOOKING FOR BAND MEMBERS

498
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:35,960
Shit. Don't tell me you two
are entering the music contest.

499
00:39:36,040 --> 00:39:38,200
You guys came at the perfect time.

500
00:39:38,280 --> 00:39:40,680
Here. Where are your phones?
Join my band right now.

501
00:39:41,280 --> 00:39:43,000
No. No, buddy. No.

502
00:39:43,560 --> 00:39:47,720
You should find someone else.
Don't let us drag you down.

503
00:39:47,800 --> 00:39:49,360
Jinnie's right.

504
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:51,360
We'd better stick to drawing.

505
00:39:51,440 --> 00:39:53,600
We're not good at that stuff.

506
00:39:54,200 --> 00:39:57,000
But don't worry, man. Someone will apply.

507
00:39:57,080 --> 00:39:59,920
- You two are both handsome.
- Good luck. See you.

508
00:40:06,960 --> 00:40:07,880
Excuse me.

509
00:40:07,960 --> 00:40:11,160
- Hey. Are you here to apply for the band?
- Yes.

510
00:40:11,240 --> 00:40:13,440
- Here. Fill this out.
- There!

511
00:40:16,160 --> 00:40:19,120
I found them. Krit and Mochi. Thank you.

512
00:40:28,040 --> 00:40:29,120
Jeez!

513
00:40:30,440 --> 00:40:32,600
Do you think anyone will actually apply?

514
00:40:37,360 --> 00:40:39,720
Okay, then let's try this.

515
00:40:41,120 --> 00:40:44,480
If we can't find applicants ourselves,
we'll have to rely on the universe.

516
00:40:48,160 --> 00:40:49,200
How?

517
00:40:54,240 --> 00:40:56,640
"A moonlight-bathing ritual
to ward off bad luck."

518
00:40:56,720 --> 00:40:59,400
Now, who wrote this?

519
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:02,600
MOONLIGHT-BATHING RITUAL

520
00:41:02,680 --> 00:41:03,680
Hey!

521
00:41:04,200 --> 00:41:05,160
Where did you get that?

522
00:41:09,360 --> 00:41:12,040
<i>Moonlight-bathing ritual</i>
<i>to ward off bad luck.</i>

523
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:16,080
<i>I'm too scared to try it.</i>

524
00:41:16,720 --> 00:41:17,840
<i>What should I do?</i>

525
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:19,640
<i>I don't want Grandma to suffer</i>
<i>because of me again.</i>

526
00:41:24,160 --> 00:41:25,800
Did you ever try it as a kid?

527
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:28,800
No. I was too scared.

528
00:41:29,560 --> 00:41:30,760
Then it's time to try.

529
00:41:31,400 --> 00:41:34,840
It'll drive away your bad luck, and people
will finally dare to join your band.

530
00:41:34,920 --> 00:41:38,200
You want me to get naked? No way.

531
00:41:41,600 --> 00:41:44,040
Whoa, this is destiny.

532
00:41:44,760 --> 00:41:46,240
It's a full moon tonight.

533
00:41:47,400 --> 00:41:48,720
I think you should try it.

534
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:51,040
No.

535
00:41:51,120 --> 00:41:53,720
Come on. You'll feel better.

536
00:41:54,360 --> 00:41:57,360
I want you to make it
into the contest too. Please?

537
00:41:58,400 --> 00:41:59,680
- Please.
- How about this?

538
00:41:59,760 --> 00:42:02,920
- You jump, I jump. Deal?
- Huh?

539
00:42:19,560 --> 00:42:21,000
I did some research.

540
00:42:21,880 --> 00:42:26,240
It says we have to bathe in the moonlight
for at least nine minutes.

541
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:30,280
And while we're at it,
we have to make a wish too.

542
00:42:30,360 --> 00:42:31,440
Are you ready?

543
00:42:33,440 --> 00:42:34,920
Fine. Let's do it.

544
00:42:36,120 --> 00:42:37,200
Come on.

545
00:42:37,280 --> 00:42:38,280
- Start!
- Start!

546
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:50,480
Are you ready?

547
00:42:51,280 --> 00:42:52,120
Yeah.

548
00:42:53,560 --> 00:42:55,160
But don't you dare peek.

549
00:42:55,760 --> 00:42:57,280
Same goes for you.

550
00:42:59,080 --> 00:43:01,800
- Three, two, one.
- Three, two, one.

551
00:43:16,360 --> 00:43:20,320
One, two, three.

552
00:43:20,400 --> 00:43:21,320
Hey, who's up there?

553
00:43:23,240 --> 00:43:24,280
- Shit.
- Shit.

554
00:43:25,680 --> 00:43:26,960
Let's move.

555
00:43:59,400 --> 00:44:01,600
<i>Emergency assembly.</i>
<i>Everyone to the first floor now.</i>

556
00:44:03,680 --> 00:44:04,760
Roger that.

557
00:44:24,720 --> 00:44:26,240
Don't forget to make a wish.

558
00:44:27,280 --> 00:44:28,760
Okay. You lead.

559
00:44:42,440 --> 00:44:45,880
May the moonlight shining down tonight…

560
00:44:46,760 --> 00:44:49,680
"May the moonlight shining down tonight…"

561
00:44:51,240 --> 00:44:54,720
…cleanse Khobfa of every bit of bad luck.

562
00:44:55,320 --> 00:44:58,800
"…cleanse Khobfa
of every bit of bad luck."

563
00:45:02,640 --> 00:45:06,440
And please let the person standing
in front of me become my boyfriend.

564
00:45:43,360 --> 00:45:45,040
<i>These guys are your bandmates?</i>

565
00:45:45,120 --> 00:45:46,320
<i>Can they even play instruments?</i>

566
00:45:46,400 --> 00:45:48,520
<i>Our band members never back down.</i>

567
00:45:48,600 --> 00:45:49,680
<i>No wonder they're your friends.</i>

568
00:45:49,760 --> 00:45:51,960
<i>The competition hasn't even started.</i>
<i>He's so good.</i>

569
00:45:52,040 --> 00:45:52,920
<i>That's so cool.</i>

570
00:45:53,000 --> 00:45:54,520
<i>I'm going all out in the final round.</i>

571
00:45:54,600 --> 00:45:55,600
<i>Same here.</i>

572
00:45:55,680 --> 00:45:57,360
There's no way I'll lose to you.

573
00:45:57,440 --> 00:45:59,720
<i>If I win, will you be my boyfriend?</i>

574
00:45:59,800 --> 00:46:01,560
<i>You've got me cheering you on.</i>

575
00:46:01,640 --> 00:46:03,200
<i>Are you really not going to keep fighting?</i>

576
00:46:03,280 --> 00:46:05,840
Why is the cure for the curse here?

577
00:46:05,920 --> 00:46:08,160
<i>I secretly put our story</i>
<i>into the song too.</i>

578
00:46:08,240 --> 00:46:10,440
<i>My boyfriend really knows</i>
<i>how to fill me with positivity.</i>

579
00:46:10,520 --> 00:46:11,840
<i>Can I kiss you?</i>
